{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "traer-backend-collection-v3",
    "name": "Traer Backend API",
    "description": "Postman collection synced with cmd/api/main.go and internal handlers.\n\nLIVE ROUTES (10): GET / | POST /login | POST /users | POST /logout | POST /jobs/create (auth) | GET /jobs (auth) | PUT /users?id= (auth) | DELETE /users?id= (auth) | GET /users/id?id= (auth) | GET /users/email?email= (auth).\n\nJob creation: POST /jobs/create accepts {urls, content_type, process_type, audio_quality?, video_quality?}. content_type is audio or video; process_type is download or upload. For audio, audio_quality may be mp3 or m4a. For video, video_quality may be 360p, 480p, 720p, 1080p, 1440p, or 2160p. URLs must be valid YouTube URLs; playlist URLs are expanded into individual jobs.\n\nAuth: POST /login sets an HttpOnly `token` cookie for 24 hours. Postman persists it and sends it with authenticated requests. POST /logout clears it.\n\nOrder: Register User -> Login -> Create Job -> List All Jobs -> User operations.\n\nThe disabled job-status, retry, download, and worker-instance endpoints remain in this collection as reference requests and return 404 until their routes are registered.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Base URL of the Traer API; do not add a trailing slash."
    },
    {
      "key": "jobId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Job ID used only by the disabled reference requests. POST /jobs/create does not return job IDs."
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "User ID used by user update/delete/lookup requests (must be numeric; backend parses with strconv.Atoi)."
    },
    {
      "key": "userEmail",
      "value": "test@example.com",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Email used by register/login/lookup requests."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Server Health Check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ""
              ]
            },
            "description": "Checks that the server is reachable. The supplied collection describes this as returning HTTP 200."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Health endpoint responds successfully', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 204]);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "description": "Public authentication and registration endpoints.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register User",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public registration (POST /users, no auth). Handler: HandleCreateUser. Requires {email, password} per CreateUserRequest; extra `username` field is IGNORED by code. Returns 201 {\"message\":\"User Signup successfully\"}; 409 if email exists; 400 if email/password empty.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"ChangeMe123!\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public login (POST /login, no auth). Handler: HandleLogin. Body {email, password} per LoginRequest — `username` is NOT read by code (only req.Email). Returns 200 {\"message\":\"login successful\",\"user_id\":\"<uuid>\"} + HttpOnly `token` cookie (24h). Cookie jar auto-saves it for auth requests. 401 = invalid credentials.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"ChangeMe123!\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "logout"
              ]
            },
            "description": "POST /logout — PUBLIC in main.go (no AuthMiddleware) but requires existing `token` cookie: 401 {\"error\":\"not authenticated\"} if missing; else 200 {\"message\":\"logout successful\"} and clears cookie. Send with cookie jar after login."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Users",
      "description": "Authenticated user-management endpoints.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get User by ID",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/id?id={{userId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "id"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{userId}}",
                  "description": "User ID to look up."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "AUTH (token cookie). GET /users/id?id= — confirmed in HandleGetUserByID (r.URL.Query().Get(id), strconv.Atoi, must be >0; 400 invalid user ID otherwise). NOTE: DB stores UUID strings so numeric lookup fails for real users. 200 returns full user row incl. password_hash; 404 user not found."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get User by Email",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/email?email={{userEmail}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "email"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "email",
                  "value": "{{userEmail}}",
                  "description": "Email address to look up."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "AUTH (token cookie). GET /users/email?email= — confirmed in HandleGetUserByEmail (r.URL.Query().Get(email); 400 email is required if empty). 200 returns full user row; 404 user not found."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update User",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users?id={{userId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{userId}}",
                  "description": "User ID to update."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "AUTH (token cookie). PUT /users?id= — confirmed in HandleUpdateUser (?id= via strconv.Atoi, must be >0; 400 invalid user ID). Body is UpdateUserRequest but ONLY password is persisted; username ignored. Success returns User updated successfully.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"password\": \"NewChangeMe123!\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete User",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users?id={{userId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{userId}}",
                  "description": "User ID to delete."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "AUTH (token cookie). DELETE /users?id= — confirmed in HandleDeleteUser (?id= via strconv.Atoi, must be >0; 400 invalid user ID). No body. Success returns User deleted successfully."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Jobs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Job",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"urls\": [\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ\"],\n  \"content_type\": \"audio\",\n  \"process_type\": \"download\",\n  \"audio_quality\": \"mp3\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/jobs/create",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "jobs",
                "create"
              ]
            },
            "description": "AUTH (token cookie). POST /jobs/create accepts {urls, content_type, process_type, audio_quality?, video_quality?}. urls contains one or more YouTube URLs and playlist URLs are expanded into individual jobs. content_type is audio or video. process_type is download or upload. For audio, audio_quality is optional and must be mp3 or m4a when supplied. For video, video_quality is optional and must be one of 360p, 480p, 720p, 1080p, 1440p, or 2160p when supplied. Returns 200 with a JSON string."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Create job returns a successful HTTP status', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 202]);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code >= 200 && pm.response.code < 300) {",
                  "  pm.test('Create job response body is present', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  });",
                  "} // This endpoint does not return job IDs."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List ALL jobs",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/jobs",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "jobs"
              ]
            },
            "description": "AUTH (token cookie). GET /jobs returns a 200 array of process rows: {id, user_id, url, status, process_type, retries, uploaded, temp_path, created_at, updated_at}. Status is one of not_started, download_queued, download_running, download_completed, download_failed, upload_queued, upload_running, upload_completed, or upload_failed."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('List jobs endpoint responds successfully', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.within(200, 299);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code >= 200 && pm.response.code < 300) {",
                  "  pm.test('Response is valid JSON', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(function () { pm.response.json(); }).to.not.throw();",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
